  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader on iPhone, I want the side margins of the card lists to follow the list density setting, so that the compact density gives the text more of the screen width.\n\n### Context\nOperator, device test 2026-11-11 (iPhone, Favoris): the side margins are very wide. Two margins add up, about 36 pt from the screen edge to the text:\n- **Outer margin, card to screen edge (~20 pt):** the system margin of `.listStyle(.insetGrouped)`, larger on large iPhones.\n- **Inner margin, card edge to text (16 pt regular / 12 pt compact):** `ListDensity.rowInsets` (`App/SwiftHFR/Settings/ListDensity.swift:18-23`), taken from legacy (`HFRswift/Swift/Favorites.swift:429` @ `87fe0d1c`). Legacy uses the same inset-grouped list, so it has the same wide margins.\n\n### Decision (operator, 2026-11-11)\nTie the margins to the density setting:\n- **Regular:** keep today's margins.\n- **Compact:** both margins about halved:\n  - outer margin about 10 pt, through `.contentMargins(.horizontal, …, for: .scrollContent)`;\n  - inner margin about 6–8 pt.\n\nThis is a deliberate difference from legacy, so the PR carries a `gap-new` ledger row.\n\n### Scope\n- Every inset-grouped card list: Favoris (Drapeaux), Catégories, a category's topic list, MP list, profile, archived drafts, and any other list using `ListDensity`.\n- One source of truth: the margins live in `ListDensity`, next to `rowInsets` and `sectionSpacing`, not per view.\n- iPad: check it still reads well (wide columns); the compact values may apply to iPhone only if iPad looks wrong, measured on screenshots.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] In compact density, on iPhone, the outer and inner margins are about half of today's; in regular density, nothing changes.\n- [ ] Changing the density in Settings updates the open lists live.\n- [ ] Swipe actions, unread badges, selection highlight and section headers (the category title tap, #769) still align with the narrower margins.\n- [ ] Tests on `ListDensity`'s values; screenshots for both densities, light and dark, iPhone and iPad.\n- [ ] Ledger row `gap-new` in the PR body; checked on device by the operator.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
